# Third-party copyrighted sound assets (Zelda Navi clips for boot
# chimes/notifications, moved into audio/zelda/ 2026-08-16) -- never
# commit these to this public repo, including the fetch script itself
# (kept local-only out of an abundance of caution about anything
# tooling-related to redistributing copyrighted assets).
audio/zelda/
audio/grab_navi_sounds.sh

# Same reasoning, root-level -- tutor_mode.py's original (now
# superseded by audio/yays//audio/nopes/, see below) wrong-key sound
# effect (nope.wav) isn't under audio/, so the rule above doesn't
# catch it.
/*.wav

# audio/yays/ and audio/nopes/ (Tutor/Simon feedback recordings,
# 2026-08-16) are the user's own recordings and are NOT ignored --
# committed on purpose, unlike the copyrighted Zelda clips above. Do
# not add a blanket audio/**/*.wav or similar rule here, it would
# catch these too.

# Pre-normalization backups of the yays/nopes recordings above (kept
# locally as a safety net while tuning playback level, see git
# history) -- superseded duplicates, not read by any code, no need to
# carry both versions in the repo.
audio/nopes/originals/
audio/yays/originals/

# Personal song transcriptions for play_melody.py -- these encode a
# specific copyrighted melody's actual notes, unlike the generic
# player tool itself. Whole directory ignored (not filename-specific)
# so moving/renaming a transcription file can't accidentally land it
# somewhere trackable -- that happened once already with a filename
# rule. Keep local-only, same reasoning as the audio/*.wav rule above.
audio/songs/

# Personal Tutor-mode songs (tutor_songs.py's load_user_songs()) --
# same reasoning as audio/songs/ above, own directory rather than
# folded into that one since the file format/contract differs (a
# Python module tutor_songs.py imports at runtime -- module-level
# NAME/SCORE/PROMPTS -- not a play_melody.py-style transcription).
# README.md is the one tracked exception: it's format documentation,
# not song content, safe to publish.
user-songs/*
!user-songs/README.md

# Local font files for future OpenSCAD wordmark-emboss work (floated
# 2026-08-31, not started) -- Fredoka's TTFs, not needed by anything
# tracked yet.
Fredoka/

# Personal custom soundfont builds (baritone uke mic/piezo, started
# 2026-09-04) -- experimental .sf2 instrument files built in Polyphone
# and copied to plink for real-hardware listening tests, not finished
# assets ready to commit. Not wired into audio_engine.py's FONTS list
# yet either (still hardcoded to the single GM soundfont).
audio/*.sf2

# Personal reference photos, not case-model assets (unlike e.g.
# enclosure/fan-dimensions.jpg or hardware/speaker_specs.jpeg, which
# ARE tracked and stay that way -- this rule is deliberately
# filename-specific, not a blanket enclosure/*.jpg or hardware/*.jpg,
# so it doesn't swallow those).
enclosure/Screenshot 2026-08-24*.png
hardware/partial_cabling_layout.jpg

# Superseded thin-wall experiment leftovers (plonk/thinner-walls-
# experiment, deleted 2026-09-02 -- see case-design.md's "Real failure
# this caught" note) -- kept locally, not published.
enclosure/chromacade-blank-side-thinner-designed.scad
enclosure/fixed_thinner.stl
